# Environment & secrets
.venv/
.env

# Data. Everything under data/ is regenerated by the scripts and stays local,
# except the seven files the dashboard (Streamlit/us_county_explorer.py) reads:
# they are committed so the app runs straight after cloning (Census Bureau
# delivery guidance, 2026-10-31). Refresh them with the four dashboard pulls.
# The * + ! pattern keeps the .gitkeep placeholders, so the folders survive a clone.
data/raw/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/raw/acs5_2024_usdash_county.parquet
!data/raw/acs5_2024_usdash_state.parquet
!data/raw/acs1_2024_usdash_county.parquet
!data/raw/acs5_2024_usdash_alloc_county.parquet
!data/raw/geo_2024_usdash_county_simple.parquet
!data/raw/geo_2024_usdash_state_simple.parquet
!data/raw/rucc_2023_county.parquet
data/processed/*
!data/processed/.gitkeep

# Python cruft
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Office lock files (created while a .pptx/.docx is open — never data)
~$*

# Product scope tool (tools/product_scope.py)
# The API catalog cache is regenerated on every run; the review file is
# team-owned state and IS committed, and so is the generated product_report.html
# (the final snapshot, so the catalog can be browsed without running the tool).
# The --export csv/xlsx outputs are script output — regenerate on demand.
scope_field_cache.json
# File-only second catalog layer - ~6,000 slimmed data.gov CKAN records,
# fetched once via `python tools/product_scope.py --pull-file-catalog`.
# Regenerable from data.gov; a fetch-failure stub (marked "stub": true)
# may sit here on machines without internet access.
file_catalog_cache.json
product_review.csv
product_review.xlsx
# Diff snapshot - captures per-product state so successive runs can show
# 'since last regeneration' deltas on the Home tab. Regenerable on every run.
.product_scope_last_run.json
# Phase 3 sample cache - actual data slices for candidate products (EDA on
# API-fetched rows). Local-only because a sample is a moment-in-time slice
# against a rate-limited endpoint; if two teammates need it, each runs their
# own `python tools/product_scope.py --repo . --sample`.
scope_data_cache.json
# Phase 3 EDA diff - written by --sample --refresh, consumed by the next
# regen so the diff banner can flag data drift alongside repo drift.
.scope_last_eda_diff.json
# Phase 4 warm-cache batch summary - counts + path lists from the last
# --warm-cache run. Consumed by the cache-coverage header and Quick Look's
# 'non_api' detection so both survive a session restart.
.warm_cache_last_run.json
# Phase 5 last-regen timestamp - read by the auto:repo insight collector to
# scope `git log --since=<T>` to the window since the previous run. Written
# at end of every regen. Local-only; not shareable state.
.product_scope_last_regen.json
# Phase 5 review-lock companion file (fcntl.flock target so the --review CLI
# helper, --warm-cache, and regen serialize their writes to
# product_review.json). Byte content is empty; only the file's exclusive
# lock is used. Also the temp file the atomic-rename writer stages under
# (.product_review.json.tmp.<pid>).
.product_review.json.lock
.product_review.json.tmp.*
# Beginner-UX pass commit #5: dev-only smoke-test artifacts from the notes/
# ingestion flow. The dev container can't unlink these files, so this pattern
# keeps them out of the commit while leaving them harmless on disk.
notes/ingested/test_beginner_ux_flow*
# Phase A 2026-07-26 commit #2: Bureau press-release mini-feed cache.
# Refreshed every 24h on regen from https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases.xml.
# Local-only; regen fetches fresh copy so caching another teammate's cache adds
# no value and would just churn.
.census_press_cache.json
